    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWhen the JIT cache dir or one of its parents is a symlink, the build cache never hits for header-only modules (the `load_jit` default): every new process compiles them again. Found with the cache on a Modal volume, which Modal mounts behind a symlink.\n\n`_to_entries` resolves each dependency but checks it against the unresolved `build_dir`, so the generated `cuda.cu` or `main.cpp` in `.staging-<uuid>/` is recorded in `sgl_deps.json` instead of dropped. `_publish` then renames the staging dir to the leaf, the recorded file is gone, and `find_prebuilt` skips the leaf. A relative `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DIR` has the same problem.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `cache.py`: `_to_entries` resolves `build_dir` before comparing. For an absolute cache dir without symlinks this is the same path, so existing caches keep hitting.\n- `test_jit_cache.py`: a CPU regression test that reaches the build dir through a symlink in `tmp_path` and passes the generated unit as the relative `cuda.cu` the depfile records. `python3 test/registered/unit/kernels/test_jit_cache.py` gives 1 failed, 42 passed on `main` and 43 passed with this change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nNot applicable: no kernel or model output changes.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nOn Modal, the first Marlin MoE call took 226 to 317 s in every container, and about 1 s with the cache dir passed through `os.path.realpath`.\n\nOn CPU (macOS), loading a header-only C++ module in three processes with the cache dir behind a symlink compiled it three times on `main`, with each later load logging `Rebuilding JIT module ...: abs:.../.staging-<uuid>/main.cpp changed` under `SGLANG_JIT_CACHE_DEBUG=1`. With this change it compiled once and the next two loads hit.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40036474344](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40036474344)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40036474291](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40036474291)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40036474397](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40036474397)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
